5. AUTOMATIC DATE, DAY AND CALENDAR SYSTEM
==================================================

THIS IS A MANDATORY FEATURE.

Implement a fully automatic date and day system across the website.

Official publication timezone:
Asia/Kolkata (IST, UTC+05:30).

The masthead must automatically display:

- Current weekday.
- Current date.
- Current month.
- Current year.

Example:

MONDAY | 4 JANUARY 2027

This is an illustrative example. Always display the actual current date.

The system must:

1. Automatically detect the current date.
2. Automatically identify the correct weekday.
3. Update the date at midnight IST.
4. Update month and year automatically.
5. Handle leap years.
6. Handle different month lengths.
7. Avoid UTC date-shift errors.
8. Work on desktop, tablet and mobile.
9. Require no manual date editing.
10. Use a reusable date utility throughout the application.

Use timezone-aware date formatting with Intl.DateTimeFormat and the IANA timezone Asia/Kolkata.

Store timestamps consistently and display them in the publication timezone.

Prevent server/client hydration mismatches.

Create a professional date bar below the masthead.

Example:

MONDAY
4 JANUARY 2027
INDEPENDENT DIGITAL NEWSPAPER

The location label, if displayed, must be configurable.

IMPORTANT DISTINCTION:

The current calendar date must update automatically.

Historical article dates, newspaper edition dates and magazine publication dates must never change when the calendar advances.

